vocabulary engine "assemblyai" only. Words and phrases to expect — product names, people, identifiers. Trimmed, de-duplicated keeping the first spelling, and capped at 1000 terms with the cap named in note. Refused by name with engine "apple".
speakers engine "assemblyai" only. Ask for speaker labels (default false); a change of speaker then starts a new cue, and with style subtitles each speaker's cues take their own colour (white, yellow, cyan, green in order of first appearance, then again; a speaker is a label within one media file). Refused by name with engine "apple".
refresh engine "assemblyai" only. Ignore the cached transcript and upload again (default false). Refused by name with engine "apple", which has no cache.
language A language tag, e.g. en-US. WITH apple: this Mac's own language by default. The two ways a tag can be wrong are two different problems with two different fixes, so they are refused SEPARATELY and the message says which you have. A tag speech recognition has never heard of is a misspelling: it is refused with the tags it does know. A tag it knows whose on-device MODEL is not installed on this Mac is refused as not installed, with the languages ready here: a person has to install it from the Generate Captions sheet, and this tool never downloads. WITH assemblyai: "auto" (the default) detects it and the result reports what was detected and how sure it was; a code is passed through unchecked, and one AssemblyAI does not support comes back as its own sentence after the upload.
